      "source": "sections/sec-000-将乙型肝炎疫苗纳入国家免疫规划.md",
      "source_hash": "eef13a9b2f9eaeb2836350d21b5c04a3cdd2aaba71c2db28b9892a92f89ba14f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The Chinese edition of the WHO note on introducing hepatitis B vaccine into national immunization programmes, explaining the global burden of hepatitis B and WHO's recommendation for routine infant vaccination. It sets out immunization strategies, including a birth dose where perinatal transmission is common and catch-up vaccination only in lower-endemicity countries. It describes monovalent and combination formulations and three schedule options tied to DTP doses. It also covers injection sites, injection equipment and a schedule table, and closes with the document number and WHO contact details.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        },
        {
          "text": "世界卫生组织关于将乙型肝炎疫苗纳入国家免疫规划的说明的中文版，介绍乙肝的全球负担以及世界卫生组织关于对婴儿常规接种的建议。文中阐述免疫策略，包括在围产期传播常见的地区接种出生剂次，并且只在流行程度较低的国家开展补充接种。介绍单价型和联合疫苗剂型，以及与DTP剂次相结合的三种接种程序选择。还涉及注射部位、注射器材和一张接种程序表，最后是文件编号和世界卫生组织联系方式。",
          "lang": "zh",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
